{{! Comments disappear from the output; standalone comment lines leave no blank line. }}
1. Variables, dotted names and escaping
Hello {{user.name}} from {{project}}!
Escaped: {{html}}
Raw: {{{html}}} | {{&html}}
{{! Missing values render as empty strings by default. Only use raw tags for trusted content. }}
Missing: [{{missing}}]

2. Sections, lists and inverted sections
{{! Objects become the current context; missing names fall back to parent contexts. }}
{{#user}}
User: {{name}} (project: {{project}})
{{/user}}
{{#enabled}}Enabled.{{/enabled}}{{^enabled}}Disabled.{{/enabled}}
{{#services}}
- {{name}}:{{port}} (project: {{project}})
{{/services}}
{{! A dot refers to the current item, useful for lists of strings or numbers. }}
Tags:{{#tags}} {{.}}{{/tags}}
{{! Inverted sections render for false, null, missing values or empty lists. }}
{{^alerts}}No alerts.{{/alerts}}

3. Reuse: partials, dynamic names and inheritance
{{! Partial paths are relative to this template; standalone partials inherit indentation. }}
Static partial:
  {{>card}}
{{! The asterisk looks up a partial name in the data instead of using a literal filename. }}
Dynamic partial:
  {{>*partial}}
{{! A parent expands a template and overrides named blocks; other blocks keep their defaults. }}
Parent with a block override:
{{<card}}
{{$body}}Custom body for {{user.name}}.{{/body}}
{{/card}}

4. Changing delimiters
{{=<% %>=}}
Hello <%user.name%>; {{user.name}} is now literal.
<%={{ }}=%>

5. Lambdas (optional; this project's YAML binding runs Bash)
{{! Interpolation calls with no arguments; sections pass raw text as $1, then render the result. }}
Interpolation: {{greeting}}
Section: {{#wrap}}Hello {{user.name}}{{/wrap}}

6. Indented interpolation (project extension)
{{! Continuation lines align with the tag's position in the rendered output. }}
note: {{|note}}

7. Conditional branches (project extension)
{{! The right operand is literal text, not a data lookup. Operators: ==, !=, =~, !~. }}
{{?if environment==production}}
Production settings.
{{?elif environment=~^qa}}
QA settings for {{environment}}.
{{?else}}
Development settings.
{{?fi}}
